  "correction": {
    "issued": "2026-08-24",
    "note": "This edition replaces the original Run #14 briefing. Four items failed a newly built verification gate and were removed or corrected: the Callosum round was not a female founder story, the Merav Bahat Israeli AI fund was a repeat of the June 29 lead, the Fortune Global 500 women CEO item was 21 days old, and the 0.8 percent US VC figure could not be traced to a primary source.",
    "corrections": [
      "Callosum was founded by Danyal Akarca and Jascha Achterberg. No female founder. Round size was $100 million, not GBP 73.5 million as a female founder win.",
      "The Merav Bahat Israeli AI fund ran as the lead headline on 2026-06-29 and was republished with no material change.",
      "The Fortune Global 500 record of 34 women CEOs was published 2026-08-03, outside the seven-day window.",
      "The 0.8 percent figure came from a reposted newsletter. Verified primary readings are 1.1 percent for FY2025 (PitchBook-NVCA, down from 2.1 percent) and 0.6 percent of deal value in Q1 2026."
    ]
  }
